{"c":[{"id":"b49778a23660a963","sum":"A1: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 input tokens and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts), the heads 'reading' question confirms it, and ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102251Z-3a116bbdf83faf20","text":"A1: free Laya (gateway, boundless) 422s any request over ~512 input tokens (489 ok, ~519 not) and allows 5 req/min per team; heads and corpus fill requests are ~2000 tokens, so the Ask path cannot run on Laya as built (evidence/screen/a1/laya-limits.txt).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102251Z-6d4e95952b64681c","text":"A1: Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts; any unread word means no reading); the heads 'reading' question confirms it and intent.agreed skips confirmScope/sectionScope. ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bb813feffb3f3c1","sum":"R1: free Laya 422s JSON-object state and choice options over ~300 chars, so Ask-led evals there mostly fail; helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs eval sets on Laya in the background (a 429 ends the pass); queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102855Z-241459cd7cad2754","text":"R1: free Laya gives HTTP 422 for a JSON-object state (harness.ts layaState sends JSON text) and for a choice question whose options total over ~300 chars (heads' scope: 634), so Ask-led evals on Laya are mostly rejected (evidence/screen/r1/probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102855Z-7e60ee41200b62c5","text":"R1: helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs all eval sets on Laya in the background; a 429 ends the pass and the set reruns from the replay cache. Other Laya users queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock; rejected requests replay from cache/failures.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
